{"type":"agent_end","messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Using this dataset's total farmers markets, and the census file: how many farmers markets does the U.S. have per 100,000 residents, to four decimal places? One confident sentence. Do not mention unverified facts and use tools to do any math necessary. Data sources: https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv and https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv"}],"timestamp":1786917367297},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking for farmers markets per 100,000 residents in the U.S., using two data sources:\n1. Farmers markets by state: https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv\n2. Census data: https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv\n\nAccording to the instructions in AGENTS.md, I should:\n1. First check if there are semantic models in the xorq catalog\n2. Check if any existing aliases cover this data\n3. Only ingest new data if needed\n4. Use xorq_select to get values\n5. Verify everything with xorq_verify\n6. Never do math myself - compose it into the catalog\n\nLet me start by:\n1. Running xorq_semantic_models to check for existing models\n2. Running xorq_catalog_list_aliases to see what's already there\n3. If nothing exists, I'll need to ingest both data sources\n4. Create a composed metric to calculate farmers markets per 100,000 residents\n5. Verify the result\n\nLet me start with checking what's in the catalog.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"I'll help you calculate the farmers markets per 100,000 residents. Let me start by checking what's available in the xorq catalog."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01Ckuspdt7jUFZ8kZjBvF5q5","name":"xorq_semantic_models","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01MzHJp